BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-10-03-electronics-recycling@norwood.ma
DTSTAMP:20261003T232821Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261003T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261003T140000
SUMMARY:Electronics Recycling Event
LOCATION:St. Timothy Church — Parking Lot — 650 Nichols St\, Norwood\, MA 02062
DESCRIPTION:Community electronics\, appliance and battery recycling\, plus reusable bicycles. Open to residents of all towns\; rain or shine. Part of the proceeds benefit St. Timothy Parish.\n\n$5 each: Computer towers\, laptops\, DVD players\, VCRs\, small printers\, stereos\, radios\, alarm clocks\, speakers\, video game consoles\, table lamps\, fans\, hair dryers\, curling irons\, projectors\, power tools\, drills\, cameras\, clocks\, trophies\, frying pans\, holiday lights and other small electronics.\n\n$10 each: Small household appliances\, vacuum cleaners/Roomba\, toaster ovens\, ceiling fans\, floor lamps\, air fryers\, electric grills\, hot plates\, small radiators\, keyboard pianos\, coffee makers\, ice makers\, sewing machines\, car seats and strollers.\n\n$20 each: Flat-screen computer monitors\, microwaves\, dehumidifiers\, air conditioners\, water coolers\, large printers/copiers\, leaf blowers\, chainsaws\, heat lamps\, artificial Christmas trees\, fire extinguishers and empty propane tanks.\n\n$25 each: TVs up to 26 inches\, CRT monitors\, outdoor grills and dorm-sized refrigerators.\n\n$30 each: TVs between 26 and 35 inches\, white goods\, washing machines\, dryers\, stoves\, dishwashers\, large appliances\, large yard equipment\, treadmills\, exercise equipment\, snow blowers\, lawn mowers\, rototillers\, large generators\, motors\, water tanks and water heaters.\n\n$35 each: TVs over 36 inches\, large refrigerators and ride-on lawn mowers.\n\n$40 each: Projection TVs.\n\nFREE (cash donations appreciated): Cell phones\, reusable bicycles\, video game media and accessories\, wires\, cables\, chargers\, car/truck batteries\, DVDs\, keyboards and tablets.\n\nArrival: Follow the cones and workers' directions. Pull your vehicle as close to the truck or dumpster as possible. You may remain in your vehicle\; workers will unload your items.\n\nHard drives will be destroyed during recycling. On-site hard-drive removal is available for an additional charge.\n\nPayment: Cash preferred. Checks accepted for payments over $30.\n\nQuestions\, business cleanouts or hosting an event: Greendayrecycling.net • GreenDayRecyclingMA@Gmail.com\n\nPrices above are as supplied by the organizer\; confirm the fee for a 36-inch TV on-site.\nCost: Most items $5–$40\nSource: https://www.norwoodtownnews.com/events/348199/electronics-recycling-event
URL:https://www.norwoodtownnews.com/events/348199/electronics-recycling-event
END:VEVENT
